    "durationMs": 1198198,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete and verified. The API is built with chi 5.2.1 + pgx against PostgreSQL via `DATABASE_URL`:\n\n- `internal/store` — connection (env-driven, with startup retry), embedded SQL migrations with a `schema_migrations` ledger, and link CRUD including atomic `clicks = clicks + 1`\n- `internal/api` — POST/GET `/links`, `/links/{code}`, `/r/{code}` with URL/code validation (422), duplicate detection (409), 404s, JSON errors, and HTML-escaping disabled so URLs return byte-identical\n- `sh start.sh` — runs `go run ./cmd/migrate` then `exec go run ./cmd/server` on `:8000`; deps are vendored so it never installs anything\n- `README.md` — startup section with `DATABASE_URL` setup\n\nVerified end-to-end: fresh migration from dropped tables, all status codes, parallel redirects incrementing exactly once each, click counts surviving a restart, non-loopback binding, and `gofmt`/`go vet`/`go build` clean. Test data was wiped and port 8000 left free for the suite."
